@startuml fig-pseudo-ftp-passive-get-sequence
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

title Pseudo-FTP — passive_get sequence

participant "Client\n(S09_Part02C client)" as C #FFE0B2
participant "Server\n(S09_Part02B server)" as S #C8E6C9
participant "Server data\nlistener" as SL #FFF9C4

C -> S : passive_get filename + LF\n(control connection :3333)

S -> S : open FILE_ROOT/filename
S -> S : bind() + listen()\non ephemeral port Q

S --> C : framed "PORT Q"\n(control connection)

C -> SL : connect(server_ip, Q)\n(data connection)
SL -> C : sendall(1-byte length + content)
S --> C : framed "done!"\n(control connection; client consumes it)

C -> C : save to ./client-temp/filename

legend bottom
  Passive mode: the server opens a temporary listener.
  The client connects to the server on the announced port.
  This mirrors real FTP PASV/passive transfer behaviour.
  NAT still requires a reachable published data port.
  The supplied pseudo-FTP baseline runs on one host.
  Control replies use byte-count + LF + payload; data reads are exact.
endlegend
@enduml
